// boxcxx — <__bits/version_print>
//
// The one feature-test macro [version.syn] gives <print>, which it co-owns
// with <ostream> -- hence a leaf, for the same [support.limits.general]
// reason as every other version_* file (see <__bits/version_any>).
//
// 202207L is N4950's own value. libstdc++ reports 202211L under -std=c++23;
// this library pins what C++23 specifies, the same policy that keeps
// __cpp_lib_out_ptr at 202106L (see <version>).
//
// The console half of [print.fun] shipped in Ф9B-2 and the macro still could
// not be defined: P2539R4's four ostream-taking overloads did not exist, and
// <ostream> is a co-owner. They arrived in Ф31e-g-3. What remains absent is
// deliberate and documented: there are no FILE*-taking forms, because BoxOS
// has no FILE type for them to be declared against.
//
// Every block below is gated on BOXCXX_OWNS_<stem>, and this file has NO
// include guard: it is meant to be included once per owning header, each time
// defining only what that header declared it owns. [support.limits.general]
// says a macro is defined by <version> AND by the header that provides the
// feature; it does not say every header that happens to include this leaf.
// A header that answers for a feature it does not provide is answering a
// question it was not asked, so it no longer does. <version> defines
// BOXCXX_OWNS_ALL and takes the lot. Checked by tools/cxx_ftm_audit.sh.

#if (defined(BOXCXX_OWNS_ALL) || defined(BOXCXX_OWNS_print)) && \
    !defined(__cpp_lib_print)
#  define __cpp_lib_print 202207L
#endif
#undef BOXCXX_OWNS_print
